AI: Affected                                                                        

 • Deployment nginx-thrift (namespace social‑network) – Available = <none>      
   (deployment status MinimumReplicasUnavailable).                              
 • Pod nginx-thrift-6c5bcfcb8f-fwpjs – Ready = False;                           
   status.conditions[Ready].reason = ContainersNotReady;                        
   status.containerStatuses[0].state.waiting.reason = CrashLoopBackOff;         
   lastState.terminated.reason = OOMKilled (exit code 137).                     

Checked, healthy                                                                

 • All other deployments in social‑network report AVAILABLE = 1 and have no     
   restart or OOM events.                                                       
 • Init container alpine-container completed successfully (exitCode 0).         

Changed during the window for another reason                                    

 • None observed for nginx-thrift; the pod’s restarts are due to the OOM‑induced
   crash loop, not a rollout.                                                   

Root Cause                                                                      

 • The nginx-thrift container is configured with memory limits requests: 128 Mi,
   limits: 256 Mi (see deployment spec).                                        
 • During start‑up the container exceeds its limit, is OOM‑killed               
   (lastState.terminated.reason: OOMKilled), and the kubelet restarts it,       
   entering CrashLoopBackOff.                                                   
 • The pod never becomes ready, so the nginx-thrift service has no endpoints,   
   breaking any downstream microservices that depend on it (e.g., API gateway,  
   other Thrift clients).                                                       

Evidence                                                                        

 • Pod description shows Ready = False with ContainersNotReady and              
   CrashLoopBackOff (container status).                                         
 • lastState.terminated.reason: OOMKilled (exit code 137) confirms memory       
   exhaustion.                                                                  
 • Deployment status reports MinimumReplicasUnavailable.                        
 • Deployment spec lists resources.limits.memory: "256Mi" (insufficient for the 
   workload).                                                                   

Remediation                                                                     

 1 Increase the memory limits for the nginx-thrift container (e.g., requests:   
   256Mi, limits: 512Mi).                                                       
 2 Apply the updated Helm values or edit the deployment, then roll out the      
   change.                                                                      
 3 Verify the pod becomes Ready and the service regains endpoints.              

After the limit adjustment, the pod should start without OOM, exit the          
CrashLoopBackOff, and restore normal operation of the Social Network            
application.                                                                    

